That may be your problem. You shouldn't get to Sokoban _and then on_,
nor should you go to Minetown and then down to Mines' End. What you
should do is this:
- decide whether the top levels of the Mines are easy enough in this
  game;
- if so, go to Minetown and avail yourself of the resources there;
- if not, do Sokoban first and strip it of its goodies;
- whichever you did, _do not_ go on down, but go back up, and do the
  other one next;
- combine the stuff you got from both, and make the most of them;
- only once you've done both, decide whether you'll go on to Mines' End
  or (probably) do a few levels below Sokoban first.

Both Sokoban and Minetown have a lot of material which you can use to
improve your kit a lot. By pooling all of that before continuing, you
give yourself a lot more chance to reach both Mines' End and the Quest.
And once you've done both of _those_ (usually; but caveat monachus!),
the Castle beckons.

